From: Belfast Patches <belfast-patches@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 00:25:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Kerbs and walkways at the solved road heights, never over the
 road beside them

The curbs and walkways were swept along the carriageways at the heights
they were laid out at, before the structure solver moved the road decals
and the terrain under them (about 0.1 m down): curbs stood 0.25 m over the
asphalt, not 0.15. A walkway took its height from the first carriageway the
index listed within 5 m, not the nearest: beside a slip under a climbing
street its edge stood 0.4 m over the slip.

- sidewalks are built on copies of the carriageways at the solved heights
  (solvedCarriageways), and their ground graded against the same
- nearestCarriagewayAt: the carriageway whose edge is nearest, with its
  height there; walkways and their road ends take it
- a curb no higher than any road beside its line, a curb return no higher
  than the road nearest it, a walkway no higher than a curb over the street
  or a driveway beside it (again after the junctions are levelled)
- the ground under a dip no deeper than 0.04 m under the road it dips to

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

